From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:36:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 37/43] Present: the second plane (the Series S interface) is
 blended over the first (fork #1081, hand port)

Fork #1081 (5ee61f28, Kyle Soderlund): with the Series S profile the
title presents two planes, the game and its interface; only the first
was shown, so menus, loading art, subtitles and prompts were black. A
pass (compose.rs) draws the game plane to the back buffer and the
interface over it with premultiplied alpha. It runs only when a second
plane is presented. VICTORY_PLANES=0: the first plane only, as before;
VICTORY_PLANE_ALPHA=straight: straight alpha.

Hand port onto the b43 line: compose.rs as it is, the present wiring in
host.rs (the `interface` argument on Host::present, the compose pass
before the copy) and in queue.rs (the second plane's description 72
bytes on, its state put back after the present), and the mod line.
Left out: the VICTORY_ASYNC_PRESENT parts of queue.rs (send_behind,
Held::Present), which this line does not have, and the framelog timing
around present.

Not compiled when written.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 5ee61f281bc598099caaad94bfde080a5e35e307, changed)
